    "title": "A state budget that delivers for seniors - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sen Judy Schwank ,\n19 hours ago The Pennsylvania General Assembly’s greatest responsibility each year is to pass a state budget that provides the funding needed to keep our commonwealth running. This isn’t my opinion — it’s part of our state constitution. Lawmakers have an obligation to approve a balanced budget annually with a deadline of June 30, which is when the fiscal year ends. Read full article\n10",
